    "durationMs": 197035,
    "finalText": "Done — the URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. All 55 integration checks passed through the real `sh start.sh` startup path, and I confirmed links and click counts survive a server restart.\n\n**What I built** (chi v5.2.1 kept, Go 1.24.3, `database/sql` + pgx driver):\n\n- **`main.go`** — embedded SQL migrations applied before serving (idempotent, tracked in `schema_migrations`), DB connect with retry, listens on `0.0.0.0:8000` with `DATABASE_URL` from the environment\n- **`handlers.go`** — all four routes: `POST /links` (201, generated or custom code, 409 on duplicate), `GET /links` (creation-ordered `{\"items\", \"total\"}`), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 + `Location`, exactly one atomic `clicks + 1` via `UPDATE ... RETURNING`); 422 for malformed JSON/invalid URL/invalid code, JSON `{\"error\"}` bodies everywhere, byte-exact responses with no trailing newline\n- **`store.go`** — persistence layer with crypto-random 8-char codes, unique-violation retry, and an `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` duplicate check\n- **`migrations/0001_init.sql`**, **`start.sh`** (migrate + serve in foreground; prebuilt binary means no network or compile at start), and a README with startup instructions\n\nValidation details worth noting: URL returned exactly as submitted (query/fragment preserved), 4–20 char code boundaries tested, `code: \"\"` strictly rejected as 422 while absent/null generates, and GET `/links/{code}` doesn't increment clicks — only `/r/` does."
  }
